WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.565
A shielded payment can still end in a leaky checkout.

00:00:04.565 --> 00:00:10.465
ShieldCheck tests the application boundary around Zcash:
what a checkout exposes, and whether a

00:00:10.465 --> 00:00:13.837
valid payment receipt gives the wrong person access.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:22.966
Start with this synthetic capture. The analyzer finds
registered test values in standard output

00:00:22.966 --> 00:00:27.218
and telemetry, including URI encoding and a Base64
envelope.

00:00:27.218 --> 00:00:32.889
The report tells us which field appeared, where, and in
which encoding.

00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:35.251
It leaves the values out.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.715
The corrected capture has no registered findings.

00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:43.770
This is a statement about the supplied capture, not a
privacy certificate.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:48.500
The browser does not verify a payment or observe traffic
you did not supply.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.356
Remove an observation and the result becomes incomplete.

00:00:52.356 --> 00:00:58.367
A leak already found stays visible. Missing evidence
cannot turn into a clean bill of health.

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:02.500
Analysis happens locally in this browser; your input is
not uploaded.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:10.645
Now the native evidence. This recorded benchmark built a
real fully shielded payment on an isolated

00:01:10.645 --> 00:01:16.117
Zcash regtest node. Zebra confirmed it at block one
hundred and three.

00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:22.044
Twenty-four benchmark expectations passed. These are
disposable test funds, and this is recorded

00:01:22.044 --> 00:01:22.500
evidence.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:29.733
Both checkouts verify the same payment. Copying the valid
receipt wins the order in the deliberately

00:01:29.733 --> 00:01:32.925
vulnerable checkout. The corrected checkout denies that
copy.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:38.909
It requires a separate order capability, gives the
authorized holder access once, and rejects a

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:42.500
replay. Payment validity and order authority are different
checks.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:49.941
Use the same detector from the offline command line,
supply captures from your test harness, or

00:01:49.941 --> 00:01:55.297
reproduce the native benchmark from source. ShieldCheck
makes checkout regressions visible and produces

00:01:55.297 --> 00:01:59.416
a report you can share without sharing the secret values.
